# Marble Voyage design gates — run before playtest

Before a **major build** or sending Evan into **Marble Voyage / Plink**, run:

```bash
./scripts/preflight_marble_voyage.sh
```

Must exit **0**. Do not hand off on failure.

## Rules enforced (see `MarbleVoyageDesignRules.swift`)

1. **Screen real estate** — 4:3 fight/title plates fill ≥85% width on reference iPad landscape; climb chart fills ~70–92% width (art-leads tall aspect, small letterbox only).
2. **Transparent UI** — power icons (`world2_plink_power_icon_*`) must have clear corners / real alpha — no opaque card-stock backgrounds.
3. **Readable battle feed** — panel ≥160pt; body/meta fonts from the design contract (no 8–9pt transcript).
4. **Climb intro** — start at top/summit, pan ≈4s to player centered (explicit `climbCameraOffset`, not fragile `scrollTo`).
5. **VS portraits** — fox / bramble / stag figurines resolve.
6. **No-clip plates** — 4:3 Fit only; never `scaledToFill` on voyage surfaces (also `scripts/check_voyage_plate_aspects.py`).

## Physics contract (live + headless continuum)

7. **No straight-up bounce** — after peg / rail / side-wall rebound, outbound velocity must not sit inside ~14° of pure +Y (`PlinkContinuum.avoidStraightUpVelocity`). Shared by `PeggleScene` and `PlinkRoundSimulator`.

Update thresholds in **both** `MarbleVoyageDesignRules.swift` and `scripts/check_voyage_design_rules.py` together.

## Portrait tiles — vision review, not a guessed crop

Do not ship a `portraitFaceBBox` (or rely on the default top-center head box) until this passes:

```bash
python3 scripts/review_voyage_portraits.py
```

That script renders the **exact tile crop** (normalized box, then center square fill) and sends **both** that crop and the full plate to a vision model in one request. The model must say the face — eyes, nose, mouth — is in frame and centered. Quills, ears, wings, or a sliver of face at the edge is a fail. It retries with the model’s suggested box. `--apply` writes only boxes that passed.

Report: `artifacts/voyage-portrait-review/<stamp>/report.json`.

The lizard idle plate has no usable face (broken composite). It stays out of `henchmenPool` until new art passes this review.

## Opening-screen DAG (predicted stills)

Every major build / preflight also runs:

```bash
python3 scripts/voyage_opening_screen_dag.py
```

Templated contracts for predictable opening screens (`title`, `chart`, `fight`, plus `shop` / `event`). Returns **anomalies** (hard fail) and **issues** (advisory). JSON report: `artifacts/voyage-opening-dag/latest.json`. Add a future still by appending a `ScreenSpec` in that script — do not invent a parallel checker.

`./scripts/build_marble_voyage.sh` runs the DAG before `xcodebuild` (skip with `--skip-opening-dag` / `VOYAGE_SKIP_OPENING_DAG=1`).

## Stage stills after a major build (agent habit)

Evan is not the builder — **you are**. After a **major Marble Voyage / Plink build** or playtest handoff:

1. **Always remind** in the handoff (one line) that silent stage stills are available — do not wait for him to ask.
2. **Do not auto-capture** unless he requested stills / “with capture”, or you need PNGs for autonomous layout review.
3. When capturing:
   ```bash
   ./scripts/build_marble_voyage.sh --capture
   ```
   or, when the `.app` is already built:
   ```bash
   ./scripts/capture_marble_voyage.sh --skip-build
   ```
4. Open PNGs under `artifacts/voyage-capture/<stamp>/` for layout review.

Capture relaunches the app on the capture simulator (default `iPad (A16)`) — avoid yanking a device Evan is actively playing. Reminder text: `./scripts/voyage_capture_reminder.sh`. Always-on rule: `marble-voyage-capture-habit.mdc`.
